The United Nations (UN) is an international organization whose stated
aims are facilitating cooperation in international law, international
security, economic development, social progress, human rights, and the
achieving of world peace. The UN was founded in 1945 after World War
II to replace the League of Nations, to stop wars between countries,
and to provide a platform for dialogue. It contains multiple
subsidiary organizations to carry out its missions.

